{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1094031-how-big-is-the-exalted-playerbase-these-days","id":1094031,"title":"How big is the exalted playerbase these days?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-18T00:54:55-07:00","id":1094031,"title":"How big is the exalted playerbase these days?","content":"Is there anyway to find out how big the exalted player base is these days?<br /> <br /> Are sales figures from drivethrurpg of the core book publicly available? Or are there any other indicators worth checking out?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Visit me at <a href=\"http://www.bragrman.com\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Tales of Grey</i></a> - my RPG Game-Master's blog.<br /> <br /> &quot;If only I had an enemy bigger than my apathy, I could have won&quot; - <i>I gave you all,</i> Mumford &amp; Sons","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8520-capitantypo","name":"CapitanTypo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8520_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"896"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T05:34:35-07:00","id":1094091,"title":"","content":"I've never heard that DriveThruRPG publishes their sales figures. You can see that Exalted 3e Core has the Platinum Seller badge on its product page, but that only denotes that it's in the top 390 (0.6 %) in terms of sales, not how big its actual numbers are. If they disclose that somewhere else, I'd like to hear about it, though.<br /> <br /> Even so, sales translates fairly badly into players. There are groups who buy a single copy for their table and pass it around between five people, and there are people like me who put $300 on the Kickstarter and have yet to play a game. Also, without comparative figures from earlier editions, it's hard to draw conclusions about trends.<br /> <br /> Forum activity has decreased, which might imply something, but again, it's hard to know how big a percentage of the player base use the forums at all.<br /> <br /> I think it's reasonable to say that the player base is smaller, since the publication schedule has been slow lately, but in terms of real numbers, I doubt there's much publically available.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 05-18-2017, 08:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T06:29:21-07:00","id":1094103,"title":"","content":"Well outside of the internet I have literally never met an Exalted player that I didn't personally introduce to the game. Which adds up to about 10 people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T07:53:52-07:00","id":1094126,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://blog.roll20.net/post/159952619415/the-orr-group-industry-report-q1-2017\" target=\"_blank\">The roll20 numbers are quite disheartening</a> (especially considering that my various groups and GM-only &quot;games&quot; I made for the explicit purpose of testing stuff make up at least 5% of that). The widely sneered-at Cypher System has almost three times as many games, the nearly-forgotten and certainly no longer relevant Dragon Age has more than twice as many players, heck, even AD&amp;D (an edition of a game that's been dead for nearly twenty years now, publication-wise, and isn't even that popular with the OSR crowd as far as I'm aware) has more than five times as many active campaigns and players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T08:52:44-07:00","id":1094160,"title":"","content":"Some hard numbers from a subset of the playerbase are available <a href=\"http://blog.roll20.net/post/131974066335/the-orr-group-industry-report-q3-2015\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, from roll20.<br /> <br /> Specifically, Exalted is 0.2% of their games (78) and 0.84% of their players (284). If you make the assumption that this is proportional, and have figures for some other game (say, D&amp;D, at 30%/40%), you might be able to back-figure the Exalted playerbase (by multiplying by 0.84/40 = 0.021).<br /> <br /> The proportionality assumption is suspect, of course, because roll20 specifically supports D&amp;D with modules and player character sheets compared to roll20's support for Exalted which is limited to character sheets (and their excellent grid-and-token-based web functionality, which I've used to run Ex3 even with it's more liberal spacing rules). But, the same could be said about the industry at large.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T08:53:44-07:00","id":1094161,"title":"","content":"Sidereals! Also, long editing time...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T10:12:32-07:00","id":1094202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1094031-how-big-is-the-exalted-playerbase-these-days?p=1094160#post1094160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some hard numbers from a subset of the playerbase are available <a href=\"http://blog.roll20.net/post/131974066335/the-orr-group-industry-report-q3-2015\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, from roll20.<br /> <br /> Specifically, Exalted is 0.2% of their games (78) and 0.84% of their players (284).</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, now we know that the number of active campaigns on roll20 has shot up considerably from 2015 to 2017 (78 vs. 162), so that's something!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T10:19:47-07:00","id":1094208,"title":"","content":"Is roll20 even representative of the actual playing public? While I have no real numbers, I find it enlightening that Exalted is still #12 on DriveThruRPG best seller list. If Arms / DB / The Realm can get out while it is still in the top 20, I think the line is in pretty good shape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>while (horse.state == dead)<br /> {<br /> beat();<br /> }","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/830-amdramnar","name":"Amdramnar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T10:32:08-07:00","id":1094215,"title":"","content":"Not too many in my region but I would like to start a campaign.<br /> Probably the only in the City","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1887-colognian","name":"Colognian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T10:49:16-07:00","id":1094223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amdramnar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1094031-how-big-is-the-exalted-playerbase-these-days?p=1094208#post1094208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is roll20 even representative of the actual playing public? While I have no real numbers, I find it enlightening that Exalted is still #12 on DriveThruRPG best seller list. If Arms / DB / The Realm can get out while it is still in the top 20, I think the line is in pretty good shape.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can say that I know about 13 people who play Exalted that I've met IRL and none of them are involved in roll20. I'd never even heard of it before now. So it's certainly not all-inclusive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T11:21:00-07:00","id":1094233,"title":"","content":"Anecdotally it seems like Exalted isn't as popular as it was back in 2012 or so. When I would look on boards such as rpg.net or /tg/ there were often several Exalted threads going at once. These days you don't see nearly the same amount of people posting or talking about it. Heck, even just look at these forums. Back during 2nd edition, the Exalted forum used to have more threads than nearly all of the other forums on the WW site put together. That's not really the case these days.<br /> <br /> I would say the dead time between 2nd edition and 3rd edition really sapped a lot of energy out of the line, and Exalted is still in the process of rebuilding. Plus, there hasn't been a whole lot of content released since the core book. I'm sure there are plenty of people who would love to purchase new material, but it simply doesn't exist. This means there isn't a whole lot to discuss or new material to attract new fans.<br /> <br /> And of course you can't forget the whole &quot;rape&quot; debacle, the Something Awful article, etc really hurt the gameline. When I've talked about Exalted with other roleplayers quite a few of them went, &quot;The rape game?&quot; There is definitely a pretty negative perception of Exalted out there among the greater roleplaying community and that has definitely not helped the gameline in its attempts to get back on its feet.<br /> <br /> So I would say the player base for Exalted is smaller than it was 5 years ago, though again that's mostly based on anecdotal evidence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T11:26:54-07:00","id":1094235,"title":"","content":"Additionally, at 2012, the 2e gameline was basically completed. If it was going to be written it was written already. So not only was there a lot of material to draw upon, but all the empty spaces were laid bare before us. There was a LOT of homebrew in those days, either fixing things that we knew wouldn't get officially fixed, or creating things (omg, the Devil Tigers were Legion) wholesale because they didn't exist yet.<br /> <br /> Once there's enough 3e materials to start from, you'll see more homebrew activity and discussion. You'll get people who wanted to play but needed more to go on than the core. We got a big injection of adrenaline in here for many months after the core was released. I'll bet we'll see it again once we have Arms and much more so after Dragon-Blooded: What Fire Has Wrought.<br /> <br /> My 2 cents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T12:02:47-07:00","id":1094251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1094031-how-big-is-the-exalted-playerbase-these-days?p=1094233#post1094233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I would look on boards such as rpg.net or /tg/ there were often several Exalted threads going at once.</div> </div> </div> </div>And even that was something of a drawdown; there was like a seven or eight year period on rpg.net when Tabletop Roleplaying Open was basically an Exalted forum where people would very occasionally talk about other games; it wouldn't be unusual for 3/4ths or more of the total threads on the front page at any time to be Exalted ones.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T13:31:02-07:00","id":1094284,"title":"","content":"I've mainly been playing Exalted on <a href=\"http://www.rpol.net\" target=\"_blank\">www.rpol.net</a> for the last seven years, six of which I've been Storytelling. I've found that there is a lot of interest among players to join Exalted games there, but there is little to no interest in storytelling games. Also, most games die either because the Storyteller loses interest or players lose interest. That is the bane of play by post roleplaying.<br /> <br /> I've been fortunate in that regard, since I've established a solid group of four players (five including myself). We can do play by post storytelling on <a href=\"http://www.rpol.net\" target=\"_blank\">www.rpol.net</a> with daily activity because we all have a Skype chat where we let each other know when we're available to post, as well as discuss the scenes and the game. However, it has been really difficult to introduce new players to my play by post group either because new players don't want to get into a game that's already well-established and has been going on for a long time, or they have difficulty getting into the Skype chat thing that's proven to be a requirement for us to keep the game going. I've tried to get some more games going there, but they've all fallen apart because I've never managed to get new players with the same dedication as the ones I already have.<br /> <br /> As for gaming in real life at an actual table, I have a session maybe once a month. I'm, however, the only one of my friends who's actually buying Exalted material. I know one guy who pirates every rpg he plays with no respect for the content creators, and the others are merely players who want to play without needing to buy any material of their own. So out of four players, only one (me) actually purchases products.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T14:18:37-07:00","id":1094304,"title":"","content":"I do a lot of analytics and guess work to try to guess at the size of things. Let's approach this from two directions and see if the numbers make sense. Onyx Path never really releases numbers, so we are forced to us a Fermi style system to get an estimate.<br /> <br /> The E3 kickstarter had 4,368 backers. Using that, I have played with 10 other people using my copy, and nobody but me has bought a book from that group. Extending that that puts the number around 40,000. I stand by that the true number is within an order of magnitude of that, meaning its between 4000 - 400,000<br /> <br /> Let's see if we can refine that number. For AAA games I know that the conversion rate between active players and active forums users for the official forums is 1-3%. Pulling another Fermi style guess here, I and 2 others of the 11 players of current Exalted use the forums, giving us a conversion rate of 27%. I am going to reduce that number by half, because they don't really post. A conversion rate of 13.5% seems very high to me compared to the numbers I normally see, so let's treat this as a spread. The true conversion rate is somewhere between 8% and 20%. If 30% of the threads in this forum are from unique posters, we have 2,052 unique exalted posters over the life time of this forum. Applying that to our conversion rate, we get 10k-25k people that play, but don't interact with the forums. 17k is our best bet guess of that.<br /> <br /> Now we have 2 different guesses. 40k and 17k. Using the 17k to refine (average) our first guess, we get 27k active-ish exalted players. Doing a quick sanity check, 270k players is outlandish, as is 2.7k.<br /> <br /> So, somewhere around <b>27k</b> is our final answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11315-remulader","name":"Remulader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11315_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T14:37:16-07:00","id":1094309,"title":"","content":"I might be the only one in my &quot;category&quot;, but as I missed the kickstarter, I bought Ex3 as a PoD when it got available. While I don't like the majority of it, I have cherry-picked parts and will but some of the coming modules. So I will run a 2.5-ish game, and it looks like we will finalize the characters (4 players) and perhaps start a game on Sunday.<br /> <br /> Considering most of my posts here is on the Exalted forum, I guess I'm not entirely successful, but I generally tend to stay away from talking about Exalted here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T15:24:48-07:00","id":1094320,"title":"","content":"One of my former players backed the Kickstarter as a group (which is why my name is thanked as a backer), but I don't have contact with him anymore so I never received my Kickstarter copy from him. Instead I bought the POD deluxe version when it was available.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T09:06:14-07:00","id":1094580,"title":"","content":"In my experience, a lot of people have disengaged with Exalted...but then, four years of essentially letting the game line rot on the vine will do that. The Kickstarter concluded in May 2013, the core rules were released in October 2015, and unless Vance and Mince are writing like absolute gangbusters (with similar progress for layout, editing, etct) we're on track for hitting that two year anniversary with the only thing released being the quickstart. If if <i>Arms</i> makes it out by then, we still will have gone those two years without a significant release and with no other Exalted types &quot;officially&quot; playable; the old White Wolf &quot;push it out push it out push it out&quot; model wasn't great, but neither is the current release schedule.<br /> <br /> There's also those who don't like the changes made in 3e; at least two people in my group who loved playing Solars in 2e I don't even want to show the new rules to because it goes completely beyond the mechanical threshold they're willing to tolerate.<br /> <br /> And you need to consider that Exalted is (at least in my experience) an extremely difficult game to recruit for. Most people will nope out when they hit the Charms chapter. The number of people I've had reject the game line after observing the community (including this forum) is in the double digits. I don't have exact numbers, obviously, but I would say that my recruitment rate is about 5%, and generally less among other groups and game clubs that I know of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T09:15:07-07:00","id":1094582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1094031-how-big-is-the-exalted-playerbase-these-days?p=1094580#post1094580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The number of people I've had reject the game line after observing the community (including this forum) is in the double digits. I don't have exact numbers, obviously, but I would say that my recruitment rate is about 5%, and generally less among other groups and game clubs that I know of.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to be honest, this has often been a difficult point for me as well, particularly something I've observed more recently, where there are a few users who respond to a few other users with just outright rudeness whenever they see the other one post, that if I was not already a fan of the game then I would be hesitant to become one after seeing this kind of thing in the official fan community.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"left\">Elemental and dragon line descriptors and capturing device coming soon</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1131843-my-own-take-on-a-craft-rewrite-that-inclu\" target=\"_blank\">Craft Rewrite </a> W/ Points, Slots, and Charms</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1106793-2nd-circle-demon-c-al-siphar-soc-initiation-symbiosis-of-the-burning-heart-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Demon Adversaries and Related Sorcerous Initiation</a></div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1091536-seeking-thoughts-and-suggestions-on-constructing-an-organization-in-game-specifically-a-university\" target=\"_blank\">Executive Leadership</a> Organization Merrit</div> <hr /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1990-norraba","name":"norraba","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1990_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T09:15:45-07:00","id":1094583,"title":"","content":"In meatspace, the only people I know who know of or play Exalted are the ones who introduced me.<br /> <br /> The majority of my play experience was PbP, on the sister site to the old Exalted Compendium Redux, PatternSpider. That site was later annexed by another RP site, but tehre remains a small contingency of Exalted games/interest there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.rpdom.com/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.rpdom.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.rpdom.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.rpdom.com/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I haven't been an active RP participant for a few years there, but it's good to get the word out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":1542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","user":"MoroseMorgan","date":". 05-19-2017, 12:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T10:36:33-07:00","id":1094611,"title":"","content":"I'll also throw my hat into the anecdote ring about how the Exalted fanbase may (or may not) be dwindling. While my real-world group played the hell out of Exalted 1e, the hit-or-miss nature of some of 2e's products started to become a bit of a deal-breaker. Having books like Sidereals and Dreams where the charms either didn't work or shouldn't work stilted some interest in newer products. As mentioned by someone else, Infernals and Lillun also caused some uncomfortable feelings about the direction the game was heading in. And the final nail came when 3e was announced and a four year gap came. Since we weren't backers at the time (due to the aforementioned issues with some of the books put out during 2e), the game might as well have been dead and buried. By the time 3e was widely available, all interest was gone.<br /> <br /> My online groups fell to similar fates, but they also were hit with other factors. That SA article somehow never got brought up (in fact, I never heard of it until this thread), but online communities did. A lot of people I knew who played online got turned off by seeing even simple questions devolve into arguments about why X sucks more than Y, but Z is so broken the entire game and all other games ever were therefore unplayable. And because this writer or that one said this one, off-the-cuff remark, the entire game must be going in some other direction. I had a few friends who wanted to start a new game, but after looking at different communities and thinking &quot;wait, so this is my pool of people to recruit from?&quot; they chose a different game instead. Obviously it was the vocal minority being very vocal and rabid, and if that were the only thing going on then maybe they'd change their minds. But end result, they stopped playing.<br /> <br /> And then there's the local game shops in my area. Only one has an employee who has ever even heard of Exalted (&quot;that D&amp;D rip-off the Vampire guys made&quot; is about all he even knows about it). Back when Under the Rose was being given away and I wanted my own physical copy, I had to drive an hour to get it, passing six stores that catered to TTRPGs (and other things, because nobody can run a business off TTRPGs anymore) because none of them bothered to grab any copies. And even that hour-away store only gave out the one copy that day.<br /> <br /> But that's really just personal experience, so take it as you will. I still love the game, still want to play it, but like my friends I've moved on to other games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T13:31:51-07:00","id":1094662,"title":"","content":"The sheer mechanical complexity of the gameline doesn't do it very many favors. <br /> <br /> I can't tell you how many potential players I have had NOPE their way away from the table, even before getting into Charms.<br /> <br /> That was 2E, and it killed my gaming table. I managed to snag a few back, but we strictly play mortals now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T13:54:37-07:00","id":1094671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>norraba</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1094031-how-big-is-the-exalted-playerbase-these-days?p=1094582#post1094582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have to be honest, this has often been a difficult point for me as well, particularly something I've observed more recently, where there are a few users who respond to a few other users with just outright rudeness whenever they see the other one post, that if I was not already a fan of the game then I would be hesitant to become one after seeing this kind of thing in the official fan community.</div> </div> </div> </div>That has unfortunately been true of the Exalted fanbase since the beginning, perhaps starting to hit it's beginning stride with the release of the 1e Dragonblooded book. The only real difference on that that aspect of the fanbase I'd say is significantly different than before is the sort of camps that arose as a result of the Kickstarter situation and the banning in areas of Jon Chung.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T14:03:16-07:00","id":1094674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1094031-how-big-is-the-exalted-playerbase-these-days?p=1094160#post1094160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some hard numbers from a subset of the playerbase are available <a href=\"http://blog.roll20.net/post/131974066335/the-orr-group-industry-report-q3-2015\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, from roll20.<br /> <br /> Specifically, Exalted is 0.2% of their games (78) and 0.84% of their players (284). If you make the assumption that this is proportional, and have figures for some other game (say, D&amp;D, at 30%/40%), you might be able to back-figure the Exalted playerbase (by multiplying by 0.84/40 = 0.021).<br /> <br /> The proportionality assumption is suspect, of course, because roll20 specifically supports D&amp;D with modules and player character sheets compared to roll20's support for Exalted which is limited to character sheets (and their excellent grid-and-token-based web functionality, which I've used to run Ex3 even with it's more liberal spacing rules). But, the same could be said about the industry at large.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've played in many exalted games and exactly one of them actually had the game selected as Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11456-nihnoz","name":"nihnoz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11456_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T15:29:39-07:00","id":1094701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1094031-how-big-is-the-exalted-playerbase-these-days?p=1094671#post1094671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That has unfortunately been true of the Exalted fanbase since the beginning, perhaps starting to hit it's beginning stride with the release of the 1e Dragonblooded book. The only real difference on that that aspect of the fanbase I'd say is significantly different than before is the sort of camps that arose as a result of the Kickstarter situation and the banning in areas of Jon Chung.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it goes beyond that, although even that would be enough to make people feel uncomforatable, but honestly you just get very strong vibes from some people that they absolutely hate other people on here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"left\">Elemental and dragon line descriptors and capturing device coming soon</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1131843-my-own-take-on-a-craft-rewrite-that-inclu\" target=\"_blank\">Craft Rewrite </a> W/ Points, Slots, and Charms</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1106793-2nd-circle-demon-c-al-siphar-soc-initiation-symbiosis-of-the-burning-heart-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Demon Adversaries and Related Sorcerous Initiation</a></div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1091536-seeking-thoughts-and-suggestions-on-constructing-an-organization-in-game-specifically-a-university\" target=\"_blank\">Executive Leadership</a> Organization Merrit</div> <hr /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1990-norraba","name":"norraba","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1990_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T15:43:46-07:00","id":1094704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1094031-how-big-is-the-exalted-playerbase-these-days?p=1094580#post1094580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my experience\u2026 four years of essentially letting the game line rot on the vine will do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, they've <i>been</i> working at it. Just because you don't like the speed you're receiving their product doesn't mean they aren't or weren't busting their balls to get it to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T15:46:32-07:00","id":1094706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>norraba</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1094031-how-big-is-the-exalted-playerbase-these-days?p=1094701#post1094701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it goes beyond that, although even that would be enough to make people feel uncomforatable, but honestly you just get very strong vibes from some people that they absolutely hate other people on here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haven't read much lately I'm afraid. Mostly just the Ask Devs,etc and I caught the last MMN so I am pretty excited about Arms moving along, though it's the splat books I want to dive into. Sorry to hear that's been the forum vibe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T19:39:21-07:00","id":1094755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1094031-how-big-is-the-exalted-playerbase-these-days?p=1094704#post1094704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dude, they've <i>been</i> working at it. Just because you don't like the speed you're receiving their product doesn't mean they aren't or weren't busting their balls to get it to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the OP was implying the game <i><b>wasn't</b></i> being worked on, but that for four years, nothing new came out. And yeah, that's usually the sign of a game not doing very well to <i>the average person who isn't as heavily invested as most of us are</i>. They're looking at the last release, seeing a big gap, maybe hearing a new edition has been in development for a while now, comparing that to other RPGs who still put out material in their &quot;edition gaps&quot; while also having a shorter announcement-to-release period, and come to a reasonable assumption that the gameline is either in developmental hell or is dead. Yeah, we here on the forum knew the reasons, knew the game was being worked on still, knew we had a wait ahead of us, and all that. But we're not the majority of TTRPG gamers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T20:54:23-07:00","id":1094769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>norraba</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1094031-how-big-is-the-exalted-playerbase-these-days?p=1094701#post1094701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it goes beyond that, although even that would be enough to make people feel uncomforatable, but honestly you just get very strong vibes from some people that they absolutely hate other people on here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is inevitable in any forum. They probably <i>do </i>hate other people on here. And that happens elsewhere too, it's just that some other communities, people either leave or get into trouble and get kicked out of places and some forums they don't. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T23:28:21-07:00","id":1094785,"title":"","content":"I know eight people who used to play Exalted. One had to stop gaming due to personal reasons before 2E came out. The other seven were in two groups (one online one in person) with some players in both groups. I was the Storyteller for both and we played until they announced 3E was coming. In anticipation, we took a break and played Pathfinder while waiting on the new rules. <br /> <br /> The new rules came. First, the online group ended. The new rules were just not suited to online play. However, the in person game forged on. We hoped that as we got better with the rules the plodding pace of game play would ease. Our last game took place when a simple combat that would have been no problem in one of our previous campaigns ended up eating up our entire gaming session. My players admitted no one was having fun. Four players. Four different castes; each with their own focus and no one was having a good time. So, now we stand at zero. We played Godbound and like it but decided Exalted would lose something if run in those rules. Now, we're hoping Scion is good and maybe we can run Exalted in that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I used to be Median but life has made me Mean.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1753-avrjoe","name":"Avrjoe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1753_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T04:09:50-07:00","id":1094830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Avrjoe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1094031-how-big-is-the-exalted-playerbase-these-days?p=1094785#post1094785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The new rules were just not suited to online play.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are about as suited as the previous edition's in my opinion. It works if you want it to, but it requires patience. Lots of patience. <br /> <br /> If anyone wants to spectate my online game, let me know.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://rpol.net/game.cgi?gi=64341&amp;date=1495277631\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://rpol.net/images/banner-light.gif\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://rpol.net/game.cgi?gi=64341&amp;date=1495277631\" target=\"_blank\"> RPoL: [Exalted] Dawn of the Chosen </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://rpol.net/game.cgi?gi=64341&amp;date=1495277631\" target=\"_blank\"> http://rpol.net/game.cgi?gi=64341&amp;date=1495277631 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> RolePlay onLine is a custom made, free web based message board community that anyone can create a game on. It supports internal private messages, groups and multiple aliases, character sheets and descriptions, plus a game map, intro and url. Your email address is kept private and is only used for verification. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T05:07:58-07:00","id":1094837,"title":"","content":"I find Initiative easier to track than Ticks. Online I mostly play on mIRC and that just requires me to put a scoreboard in the topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T13:05:47-07:00","id":1094924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1094031-how-big-is-the-exalted-playerbase-these-days?p=1094837#post1094837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find Initiative easier to track than Ticks. Online I mostly play on mIRC and that just requires me to put a scoreboard in the topic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just a hypothetical question for you (and I don't mean to be insulting); could you easily keep track of initiative online <i>without</i> that tool? I wasn't a big fan of ticks, but at least they were fairly static. <br /> <br /> I only played 3E at a table and we had to use a similar program to keep track of initiative. We had to use an outside program to play the game. I don't think any of us would have even tried without such a tool. Even with such help, we hated it. I like combat in most games. In Exalted, I usually play the Dawn Caste, but the initiative system as presented in 3E just sapped my will to play. It. Took. Forever. <br /> <br /> Now, this was obviously just my personal experience and your mileage may vary, but I wouldn't be surprised if there were more than a few who felt similarly. <br /> <br /> I'd like to end this by saying this comes from someone who wanted nothing more than to love Exalted 3E with every fiber of his being. It just didn't love me back.<br /> <br /> At least I can look forward to the flavor of the expanded map and locations.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Map of Third Edition Creation in a First Edition Style<a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/media?url=https%3A%2F%2Fpreview.redd.it%2F18ttip13xdsc1.png%3Fwidth%3D5780%26format%3Dpng%26auto%3Dwebp%26s%3D35f3d332551385032587cde8b093e4923ed687ee\" target=\"_blank\">\u200b</a>, (<a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/media?url=https%3A%2F%2Fpreview.redd.it%2Fpjil7fcr0esc1.png%3Fwidth%3D5780%26format%3Dpng%26auto%3Dwebp%26s%3Dcfdff833d8e8afe3e86ca27c06569cad0bb44be9\" target=\"_blank\">3E Locations Only</a>) (<a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/media?url=https%3A%2F%2Fpreview.redd.it%2Fik6dit8lrlrc1.png%3Fwidth%3D5780%26format%3Dpng%26auto%3Dwebp%26s%3D0e0c488dea6e066af00d52c6d5994592bb4d8359\" target=\"_blank\">1E, 2E, 3E Amalgam</a>)\u200b<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/kashi85\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt, where I post some Exalted stuffs.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/853-kashi","name":"Kashi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar853_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T13:21:28-07:00","id":1094929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1094031-how-big-is-the-exalted-playerbase-these-days?p=1094837#post1094837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find Initiative easier to track than Ticks. Online I mostly play on mIRC and that just requires me to put a scoreboard in the topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have never use mIRC, so there can be something I'm missing. But wouldn't the same scoreboard be used for tracking Ticks? Check for the lowest number, let that person take an action and then add the number of ticks the action took, check for the lowest number... Rinse and repeat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T13:31:59-07:00","id":1094933,"title":"","content":"Tool? An mIRC topic is just a bit of text at the top of the screen rather than part of the text. <br /> <br /> All we did and have been doing since the playtest is putting people's join battle rolls in ascending order, adding 3 (or whatever) to them and noting which round it is. Then when a character suffered withering damage subtracting it from the relevant total and adding it to the attacker's. <br /> <br /> The only real learning curve for us there was a tendency to forget additional Initiative like the (+1 for hitting, +5 for crashing etc) but that's where presenting the information as a scoreboard was useful - a couple of times a player said &quot;that doesn't look right to me&quot; and we double checked, it still happens occasionally but the number of times has been decreasing. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T17:42:20-07:00","id":1094977,"title":"","content":"My experience with the system indicates that there aren't a lot of people playing it. It was hard to find people willing to play locally, even when I was the one offering to run a game. Most of the people I know who used to play felt burned by the Kickstarter and the development cycle, so it ended up being people with no or very minimal Exalted experience, and the current Core is a very hard sell to newcomers.<br /> <br /> I'd still be interested in playing a Play by Post game, but the community I most often frequent (rpol.net) has very very few Exalted games - only one 3E game has posted as looking for players this year, and only 4 last year - the year the edition was released. Back in 1E or 2E, there would usually be several starting up every month. So my own anecdotal evidence would be that there are very few players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T19:50:18-07:00","id":1094997,"title":"","content":"all of this sounds very disheartening, because if the player base decreases then to me that seems like the impetus for the company to produce more products, so considering all of this, is there a way we can try and increase the number of players?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"left\">Elemental and dragon line descriptors and capturing device coming soon</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1131843-my-own-take-on-a-craft-rewrite-that-inclu\" target=\"_blank\">Craft Rewrite </a> W/ Points, Slots, and Charms</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1106793-2nd-circle-demon-c-al-siphar-soc-initiation-symbiosis-of-the-burning-heart-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Demon Adversaries and Related Sorcerous Initiation</a></div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1091536-seeking-thoughts-and-suggestions-on-constructing-an-organization-in-game-specifically-a-university\" target=\"_blank\">Executive Leadership</a> Organization Merrit</div> <hr /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1990-norraba","name":"norraba","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1990_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T20:22:39-07:00","id":1095003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>norraba</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1094031-how-big-is-the-exalted-playerbase-these-days?p=1094997#post1094997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">all of this sounds very disheartening, because if the player base decreases then to me that seems like the impetus for the company to produce more products, so considering all of this, is there a way we can try and increase the number of players?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just give it time. Once the gameline starts releasing more content, you'll have more people getting back into the game. I know several people who like Exalted, but they simply do not like playing Solars. One of them is waiting until the Lunar book comes out before he gets back into the game. &quot;Call me when Lunars comes out,&quot; is the only thing he says when I mention Exalted to him. Another guy I know only wants Infernals. Poor bastard is in for a long wait. Right now though, they're not interested in playing Exalted and also don't want to either homebrew up their own Exalt or play someone else's homebrew. <br /> <br /> I imagine there are a fair number of other people like that out there, who don't really want to get into 3rd edition when we basically only have one book and one splat out. Plus, the long production time hasn't helped much. But once they start rolling out books, I expect the Exalted fanbase will grow, though it's tough to imagine that it will get as big as it was during the height of 2nd edition, at least anytime soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T20:30:23-07:00","id":1095006,"title":"","content":"Actually I got my Dnd/Pathfinder Gm honestly interested and excited about playing in this edition. Barely could pull that off in 2nd. I mean granted my group now consists of what is philosophically one of the Sons of Ether, a doctor, and an assassin, but still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T04:41:17-07:00","id":1095082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1094031-how-big-is-the-exalted-playerbase-these-days?p=1094929#post1094929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have never use mIRC, so there can be something I'm missing. But wouldn't the same scoreboard be used for tracking Ticks? Check for the lowest number, let that person take an action and then add the number of ticks the action took, check for the lowest number... Rinse and repeat.</div> </div> </div> </div>What bugged me about ticks was that I had to stop and update the information constantly, even if a character isn't doing anything the combat is still drawing closer to their next action.<br /> <br /> Initiative only changes when they do something and while it has the potential to flow back and forth I\u2019ve found the default is it going one way fast or two well matched parties being reluctant to concede the advantage.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T05:10:59-07:00","id":1095089,"title":"","content":"2e-style ticks also sucked in that a PC who wasn't optimizing Speed might be going <i>half as often</i> as someone who was, and that was before flurries were factored in.<br /> <br /> Whereas in 3e, everybody gets to go each round regardless, absent an effect that says otherwise, and even the speed kings probably won't be going first on <i>every</i> turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-21-2017, 08:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T05:48:41-07:00","id":1095098,"title":"","content":"As for the original topic. I attribute the lull in activity to a lack of edition content.<br /> Though this doesn't necessarily reflect who is playing the game because I've long noticed that there's very few people on these forums who talk about their characters or their games, even attempts to get people talking about their characters often meets with reluctance. It's been that way for as long as I can recall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 05-21-2017, 10:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T07:05:27-07:00","id":1095116,"title":"","content":"Shit, I <i>love</i> talking about my characters and my games, but I also have some pretty disappointing memories of having folks fling &quot;the S-word&quot; at me (that is, &quot;snowflake&quot;) over any character being even a little bit special, and even on these forums I have to remind myself that kind of ass-hattery isn't permitted before I feel up to posting about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T07:07:15-07:00","id":1095117,"title":"","content":"My experience is similar to what others have written here.<br /> <br /> I and my gaming group have played Exalted since first edition, and absolutely loved it all the way up to, well now.<br /> <br /> We spoke about it recently, and there is a kind of fatigue about it. Between the long wait - and the prospect of long waits between future releases, the sheer weight of the systems, and the drama, we are just tired of it.<br /> <br /> I think (and hope) future releases can reignite the passion, and I imagine that the perceived lull in interest may be well be people waiting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Avatar by Raven &amp; Blue Jay.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/663-aleks","name":"Aleks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar663_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T07:26:22-07:00","id":1095122,"title":"","content":"I'm about as passionate as I've always been since I discovered it. Still playing every day online and working on some kind of Exalted-related content every day. My only frustrations is that I want to do more than I have time for. I have to fight over drawing on my Exalted comic to writing on my Necromancy homebrew to writing on my Machineborn setting to working on one of my many Exigent ideas ot Exalt types ideas. My fatigue comes from passion and lack of free time to explore everything I want to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T07:52:06-07:00","id":1095130,"title":"","content":"I share many of the same observations here, Exalted is more-or-less dead except for those who were pretty interested in it prior to 3e. At the moment the only people I can get involved in the game are those who were loyal fans during the previous editions. I haven't been able to get anybody into 3e.<br /> <br /> I think the delays were part of the problem, but the real issue was the way the community sort of collapsed in upon itself. A good portion of the initial community was destroyed by openly antagonistic fan relationships and public arguments between producers and consumers. The fact that this was blamed on the 'caustic' community... which had held together just fine for almost a decade and was doing quite well previously... didn't help.<br /> <br /> Further, the same arguments that made the Exalted fandom infamous... also contributed a certain amount of energy and vitality to online discussions about the game. This meant frequent topics, frequent posts, and impassioned arguments. It also meant a great deal more homebrew because the same people that involve themselves in these arguments are usually the ones who care/understand about mechanics enough to post that stuff.<br /> <br /> Finally, in the post-delay environment criticisms and disputes that would have initially been minor were magnified. Many high profile bans of previously ubiquitous forum personalities ensued. We still haven't recovered from the damage and IMO we never well.<br /> <br /> Lessons can be taken from this in both fan interaction and forum moderation.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T08:27:07-07:00","id":1095142,"title":"","content":"{deletion}<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T09:35:27-07:00","id":1095159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1094031-how-big-is-the-exalted-playerbase-these-days?p=1094704#post1094704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dude, they've <i>been</i> working at it. Just because you don't like the speed you're receiving their product doesn't mean they aren't or weren't busting their balls to get it to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Naturally <i>I</i> know they've been working at it. And my point really wasn't about what I think; as Vysha pointed out, it comes down to perception. I'm certain that most everyone on this forum knows about the medical problems that Morke had (I don't know how to make the fancy o, sorry), but do you think that Average Joe and Jane Gamer in the comic shop did, or if they even gave a shit? <br /> <br /> To give you an idea, I act as an Exalted info source for about twenty people. Putting aside the implication right there (that I personally know twenty people who are <i>sorta</i> interested in Exalted but not enough to follow it themselves), here's a paraphrased conversation I had with one of 'em recently:<br /> <br /> Me: So Robert Vance and Eric Minton are going to be leading development on Exalted now.<br /> Him: Oh, cool. Don't know who they are. So they're doing 4th Edition now? Let me know what you think when it comes out.<br /> Me: No, it's still third.<br /> Him: Ah. Okay, then.<br /> <br /> Now I'm not so arrogant as to extrapolate this dude's attitude towards gamerdom at large, but he is a fairly good representation of John Q. Average Gamer. What really struck me about the conversation was it caused me to realize that so much time had passed since I had any Exalted news to pass to this guy that he had assumed that 3e had been canned and that new developers would mean an edition reboot. And, honestly...I can't really fault him for that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T09:42:57-07:00","id":1095163,"title":"","content":"In consideration of what we had revealed about the wait after the release of the core book, as well as at this point, well described and well mulled over Kickstarter situation. Perhaps it's time to give it a rest, even if a temporary one. We're already, in a very short period of time seeing what the new development team is doing and that parts are in the process of moving. The beaten dead horse is quite tender at this moment I imagine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":".  Don't type out sentences while house cleaning kids 05-21-2017, 02:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T10:36:42-07:00","id":1095171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1094031-how-big-is-the-exalted-playerbase-these-days?p=1095159#post1095159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I'm not so arrogant as to extrapolate this dude's attitude towards gamerdom at large, but he is a fairly good representation of John Q. Average Gamer. What really struck me about the conversation was it caused me to realize that so much time had passed since I had any Exalted news to pass to this guy that he had assumed that 3e had been canned and that new developers would mean an edition reboot. And, honestly...I can't really fault him for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes me wonder, would the game get more people interested in it if a 4 replaced the 3 on the cover?<br /> <br /> Theoretically it wouldn't change much. The gesture would be more symbolic than anything for the informed, but it might mean a great deal to the people who don't know or care about the drama enough to parse the particulars. It's a good short hand for saying 'fresh start', I suppose.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T11:30:35-07:00","id":1095183,"title":"","content":"That sounds like an excellent way to add some confusion to the current situation, and not much else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T11:47:29-07:00","id":1095190,"title":"","content":"I <i>especially</i> don't want to see a 4 on Ex3's cover, not just for the excellent reasons <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar186_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"186\" data-vbnamecard=\"186\">Morty</a> provided, but also because it's a big &quot;Fuck you&quot; to John and Holden and all their hard work\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026<i>and</i> because I have to socialize at times with a colossal asshole who thinks the funniest thing in the world is to say, &quot;Hey [Alucard], didja hear they're making an Exalted Fourth Edition now? I've already preordered it!&quot;<br /> <br /> I worry that having to see the shitty grin on his face as he mindlessly parrots it <i>and it being true</i> might drive me to violence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-21-2017, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T11:57:37-07:00","id":1095194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1094031-how-big-is-the-exalted-playerbase-these-days?p=1095183#post1095183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">..... not much else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does stroking certain people's hate boner for Holden and Morke count ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T12:14:07-07:00","id":1095202,"title":"","content":"I could be wrong about this, because obviously this is an anecdotal observation, but I think the population of people who are prospective new 3e players who know/care who specific developers were and why they ought to be loved/hated has gotta be less than 5% or something. All the hate boners are gonna be in the already sold/unsold camp, people who are familiar enough with the line and the history to not really qualify as 'noobies'. Those newcomers are the kind of people Coik was talking about, I think. Lots of the people I got interested in 2e had only the vaguest surface awareness of the line (at best) when they started up. That's a big pool of potential players. It's a shame this confusion exists, but that said, edition reboots are often more trouble than they are worth... and after considering it this afternoon and reading these replies I kinda agree that it'd be a risky move!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T12:32:26-07:00","id":1095208,"title":"","content":"The current situation of the Exalted line is less than ideal. Whose fault is that is a topic that has been argued back and forth. But doing <i>another </i>reboot is pretty much on the very bottom of things that might help. And it's a pretty short list, anyway - the devs need to actually release new material, and we need to talk about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T12:59:38-07:00","id":1095212,"title":"","content":"Threads like this sap my will to be here much more than the lull in activity from the gameline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T13:57:37-07:00","id":1095229,"title":"","content":"Ok, to lighten the mood :<br /> <br /> French ST, 8 players + myself, very enthousiasts.<br /> <br /> And we're of course hoping for the fr translation &gt;.&lt;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>French Exalt &amp; ST &amp; ToolMaker [<a href=\"http://refhi.free.fr/\" target=\"_blank\">Website</a>]<br /> Advanced Character Generator <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1087290-advanced-character-generator#post1087290\" target=\"_blank\">Thread, </a><a href=\"http://refhi.free.fr/exalted3/Fiche%20perso%20colab.xlsx\" target=\"_blank\">Excel Version</a> &amp; <a href=\"http://refhi.free.fr/exalted3/Fiche%20perso%20colab.ods\" target=\"_blank\">LibreOffice Version</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141199-exalted-3-familiar-generator\" target=\"_blank\">Familiar Generator Thread</a> &amp; <a href=\"http://refhi.free.fr/exalted3/Familiar%20Generator.ods\" target=\"_blank\">Libreoffice Version</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13355-refhi","name":"Refhi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13355_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T14:08:14-07:00","id":1095237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1094031-how-big-is-the-exalted-playerbase-these-days?p=1095212#post1095212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Threads like this sap my will to be here much more than the lull in activity from the gameline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same.<br /> <br /> I'm a French-Canadian ST, currently have 3 players, and there are at least 12 more in my vicinity. None come to the forums.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T15:36:16-07:00","id":1095265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1094031-how-big-is-the-exalted-playerbase-these-days?p=1095130#post1095130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I share many of the same observations here, Exalted is more-or-less dead except for those who were pretty interested in it prior to 3e. At the moment the only people I can get involved in the game are those who were loyal fans during the previous editions. I haven't been able to get anybody into 3e.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to counter your anecdote with an anecdote of my own and say that me and my playground had no interest in Exalted before 3e dropped. Trying to read the 2e core actually actively turned me off and left me with a really, really bad impression of the line for a long time.<br /> <br /> Of the (large number) of people I play with, only one of them besides myself was even aware of Exalted before 3e came out. Whose anecdotes scale out to the wider audience better? I don't know, because an anecdote is an anecdote, and doesn't tell anyone a damn thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11456-nihnoz","name":"nihnoz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11456_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T16:06:00-07:00","id":1095269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1094031-how-big-is-the-exalted-playerbase-these-days?p=1095212#post1095212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Threads like this sap my will to be here much more than the lull in activity from the gameline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just keep in mind that in the end, it's not terribly important how many people are playing Exalted today, as opposed to how many were playing 6 or 7 years ago. Whether there's 10 million people, or 10 thousand, the two things that matter are that that OPP is going to continue to publish Exalted books, and the fact that <i>you</i> like Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T16:24:11-07:00","id":1095278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1094031-how-big-is-the-exalted-playerbase-these-days?p=1095269#post1095269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just keep in mind that in the end, it's not terribly important how many people are playing Exalted today, as opposed to how many were playing 6 or 7 years ago. Whether there's 10 million people, or 10 thousand, the two things that matter are that that OPP is going to continue to publish Exalted books, and the fact that <i>you</i> like Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually something very reassuring to think about, and as someone who throuroughly enjoys 3rd edition and can actively see that it needs much less tweaking than previous editions, and is something that I could actually st and get a group of semi interested friends into playing, something I don't think I could have said about second. <br /> <br /> So I am going to eagerly wait for the new material and also do my part to homebrew things when I can to help advance things in the meantime, because I do greatly enjoy this game and hope to see more people enjoying it in the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"left\">Elemental and dragon line descriptors and capturing device coming soon</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1131843-my-own-take-on-a-craft-rewrite-that-inclu\" target=\"_blank\">Craft Rewrite </a> W/ Points, Slots, and Charms</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1106793-2nd-circle-demon-c-al-siphar-soc-initiation-symbiosis-of-the-burning-heart-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Demon Adversaries and Related Sorcerous Initiation</a></div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1091536-seeking-thoughts-and-suggestions-on-constructing-an-organization-in-game-specifically-a-university\" target=\"_blank\">Executive Leadership</a> Organization Merrit</div> <hr /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1990-norraba","name":"norraba","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1990_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T16:29:40-07:00","id":1095280,"title":"","content":"Plus another thing to consider is that people do have favorite factions and splats. There are probably people who are interested in playing, but are waiting for to be able to play their favorite faction without needing to homebrew everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T16:32:06-07:00","id":1095282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1094031-how-big-is-the-exalted-playerbase-these-days?p=1095130#post1095130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally, in the post-delay environment criticisms and disputes that would have initially been minor were magnified. Many high profile bans of previously ubiquitous forum personalities ensued. We still haven't recovered from the damage and IMO we never well.<br /> <br /> Lessons can be taken from this in both fan interaction and forum moderation.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIt would have been great if the lesson that &quot;the forums have rules of conduct that you agreed to abide by when you signed up&quot; had been the lesson learned when warnings were issued. Unfortunately certain people felt they were above those rules or that the rules didn't apply to them. We made it very clear that the behavior seen near the end of the old WW forums was not going to be allowed here because it absolutely drove people away from participating on those forums. I would know because I read all the reports from users who were sick of being attacked for daring to disagree with some forum superstar. Stating the moderation caused problems rather than people who couldn't engage others within the rules of conduct is absolutely bullshit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":17}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T18:03:36-07:00","id":1095308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1094031-how-big-is-the-exalted-playerbase-these-days?p=1095269#post1095269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just keep in mind that in the end, it's not terribly important how many people are playing Exalted today, as opposed to how many were playing 6 or 7 years ago. Whether there's 10 million people, or 10 thousand, the two things that matter are that that OPP is going to continue to publish Exalted books, and the fact that <i>you</i> like Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Exalted is doing great, so lots of people are clearly buying books and considering playing. I think it just has yet to hit critical mass in this edition and I strongly suspect the DB book is going to be sort of a moment of rebirth. The old community will never come back but the new community may eclipse it yet. We have our own age to write, no need to pine for the glory of the old!<br /> <br /> I should also note to give full context to the anecdotal lack of Exalted in my area that RPGs in general have completely crashed lately, not JUST Exalted. Our last game store converted into a Warhammer place a while ago and the writing is kinda on the wall that it's becoming a digital age for gamers in my region. So I wouldn't take my inability to recruit as anything close to a death knell for the line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T21:20:34-07:00","id":1095352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1094031-how-big-is-the-exalted-playerbase-these-days?p=1095194#post1095194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does stroking certain people's hate boner for Holden and Morke count ?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is something I've been oblivious to... what's the source of the hate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Visit me at <a href=\"http://www.bragrman.com\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Tales of Grey</i></a> - my RPG Game-Master's blog.<br /> <br /> &quot;If only I had an enemy bigger than my apathy, I could have won&quot; - <i>I gave you all,</i> Mumford &amp; Sons","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8520-capitantypo","name":"CapitanTypo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8520_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"896"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T21:35:32-07:00","id":1095354,"title":"","content":"Edit: Fuck it, not getting into this fight again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","user":"The Revenge of TV Head","date":". 05-22-2017, 01:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T04:40:23-07:00","id":1095439,"title":"","content":"At least in my local vincinity and in my online contact list there is a steady growing of interest. None of these people is active on the forums or other exalted online communities though.<br /> <br /> We started with 4 guys 2 years ago and now we are actively playing with 9. 2 don't have the time to play at the moment and at least 2 to 4 people I know are at least interested. There is also a completely different group of at least 4 players that play Exalted but not in a way my guys and I would like to play.<br /> Only one guy our group tried to convince to play said it was too complex for him.<br /> <br /> So yeah we went from 4 to around 20 people within 2 years. Probably more if the other group also recruited a few people. I don't think this means the game is dying. Ex3 only added to the interest since everyone got enthusiastic once again.<br /> Pretty sweet honestly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My (mostly) German Exalted blog: <a href=\"http://ryokiseck.de/\" target=\"_blank\">Praise the Spiral!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11185-ryoki","name":"Ryoki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T07:21:18-07:00","id":1095468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1094031-how-big-is-the-exalted-playerbase-these-days?p=1095308#post1095308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Our last game store converted into a Warhammer place a while ago and the writing is kinda on the wall that it's becoming a digital age for gamers in my region.</div> </div> </div> </div>The shit with Warhammer End Times and Age of Sigmar gave me so much patience for 3rd edition. At least 40k 8th edition was handled somewhat competently (i.e. mostly good but I can't call the Gathering Storm books well done + the rushed execution of them fed into the feeling that this was another End Times).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T09:38:44-07:00","id":1095517,"title":"","content":"Magic: The Gathering wounded the RPG playerbase, but it was Warhammer that took advantage of the onsought penalty and dealt a decisive blow. Exalted has actually adopted well to the digital shift, but I haven't - I haven't been able to recruit online or play online, really, so the death of the old school recruitment pool has hit my games pretty hard. When I was pulling groups five years ago I had three or four reggies, but these days It's 1-2 player games (which actually Exalted is particularly good for, as crunchy / deep systems really shine when you have fewer people at a table and can bog with a full 5).<br /> <br /> I think Exalted 3e is pretty much the best 1 on 1 fantasy game (1 ST, 1 Player) on the market. But I still wish I didn't have to play it that way. If only I could adjust to not playing face to face...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T10:21:44-07:00","id":1095537,"title":"","content":"Seems the few RPG players I have spoken to outside my little group think we are insane for playing Exalted until I explain that no it ain't the basic game it is homebrew only kind of Ex2. Those are still people that have tried Exalted in the past but where worn out while Ex3 wasn't yet in the pipeline.<br /> <br /> Another source of loss is because people find that Exalted 1-2 ed are very different beasts from Ex3 and a lot of people aren't finding what they liked in the older versions in the new edition. I'm at least partially in that camp I think initiative combat is bollocks and craft an unnecessary mini-game at the same time my homebrew steals some of the good stuff like evocations which are brilliant! and a bit of the sorcery, the most innovative charms and so on.<br /> <br /> Still even the current forum activity say that Exalted has a fairly healthy playerbase compared to most games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3085-chance","name":"chance","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T17:14:12-07:00","id":1095671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1094031-how-big-is-the-exalted-playerbase-these-days?p=1095517#post1095517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magic: The Gathering wounded the RPG playerbase, but it was Warhammer that took advantage of the onsought penalty and dealt a decisive blow. Exalted has actually adopted well to the digital shift, but I haven't - I haven't been able to recruit online or play online, really, so the death of the old school recruitment pool has hit my games pretty hard. When I was pulling groups five years ago I had three or four reggies, but these days It's 1-2 player games (which actually Exalted is particularly good for, as crunchy / deep systems really shine when you have fewer people at a table and can bog with a full 5).<br /> <br /> I think Exalted 3e is pretty much the best 1 on 1 fantasy game (1 ST, 1 Player) on the market. But I still wish I didn't have to play it that way. If only I could adjust to not playing face to face...</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you do webcam? Just saying I know roll20 does allow video feed and that might help you a bit if you need to be able to see the other people you're running with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T18:17:26-07:00","id":1095696,"title":"","content":"According to google trends the interest in Exalted has stayed fairly consistent for the last several years. Anyone who has other interesting ideas to plug into google trends let me know. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://trends.google.com/trends/explore?date=all&amp;q=exalted%20rpg,onyx%20path,rpg.net\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://trends.google.com/trends/explore?date=all&amp;q=exalted%20rpg,onyx%20path,rpg.net\" target=\"_blank\"> Error 429 (Too Many Requests)!!1 </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://trends.google.com/trends/explore?date=all&amp;q=exalted%20rpg,onyx%20path,rpg.net\" target=\"_blank\"> https://trends.google.com/trends/explore?date=all&amp;q=exalted%20rpg,onyx%20path,rpg.net </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T20:13:27-07:00","id":1095730,"title":"","content":"For further &quot;this isn't really evidence&quot; commentary, my home gaming group is about 7-9 people depending on the game and the week. The interest in Exalted, the nature of the game, and our schedules has me running two Exalted games, one with three players and one with four. We're loving it, all my players are having fun, yes the complexity can be daunting at first but we've all taken to it and we're having a blast with the new Ex3 game engine. So far everything seems to be doing what it's supposed to, encouraging the kind of play it's supposed to, and letting my players make the kinds of characters they want to. Even the oft-maligned crafting system. So add 8 enthusiastic players outside of Pittsburgh to the total.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1398-corwin859","name":"corwin859","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T01:23:00-07:00","id":1095792,"title":"","content":"Me and my group, while we loved exalted, consider the line pretty much dead and the 3rd edition extremely difficult (borderline impossible) for an ST to run with the current book(s). The same is true for another group who played exalted that we have met.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/23580224/t4q8xrt1.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/816-leo1925","name":"leo1925","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar816_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T05:57:47-07:00","id":1095862,"title":"","content":"I have 8 players (5 regulars, 3 occasionnal) in my current campaign, 4 of which had never played Exalted before Ex3. Those who have consider that edition to be superior in most points.<br /> <br /> I know at least five persons who would like to play but live too far from us to join our campaign.<br /> <br /> Edit: and to clarify, in that dozen or so of people, only three of us are KS backers, and I'm the only one I know of that hangs out on the net to talk about Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":541,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","user":"LeTipex","date":". 05-23-2017, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T07:27:27-07:00","id":1095901,"title":"","content":"I am involved with two games, one with 5 old time rpg friends and one with 3-5 family members (my wife, 2 brothers, 1 sister-in-law, and a cousin).<br /> <br /> The old timers are part of a 17-22 year old group we had since the time of AD&amp;D, GURPS, and V:tM1e. And while my brothers and cousin were exposed to RPGs, through me, they were 7-12 years younger than me, so we hadn't played together. The wives had never played, and my sister-in-law hadn't even heard of RPGs in general.<br /> <br /> None of us had any contact with Exalted before 3e. So that is 11 people who play Exalted that didn't before, out of which 8 are regulars and 3 semi-regular. I am the only one that supported the Kickstarter, and only the GM of the old timers group also bought the PDF.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 05-23-2017, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T07:45:54-07:00","id":1095908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1094031-how-big-is-the-exalted-playerbase-these-days?p=1095696#post1095696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to google trends the interest in Exalted has stayed fairly consistent for the last several years. Anyone who has other interesting ideas to plug into google trends let me know. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://trends.google.com/trends/explore?date=all&amp;q=exalted%20rpg,onyx%20path,rpg.net\" target=\"_blank\">https://trends.google.com/trends/exp...20path,rpg.net</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted 3rd seems like a good add it seems to be fairly solid over the last few years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3085-chance","name":"chance","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T12:38:27-07:00","id":1096002,"title":"","content":"I'd say my experiences largely mirror others. The only people I know who actively play Exalted are the people I play with. Of those, three were completely new to RPGs, and the other two are members of my group from way back.<br /> <br /> The events of the last few years, including the content lull, hit us kinda hard. Honestly, if we didn't already have a game in mind that was Exalted, I doubt we would be playing it now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T08:44:51-07:00","id":1096363,"title":"","content":"It was a foregone conclusion that I'd be running Ex3. Two veterans from my 8 year long 1st/2nd Ed game wanted to get back into it, and two members of our rpg circle were both very interested in learning to play. The game is going wonderfully, learning curve and all. At some point I acquired a large accountant's ledger that tracks initiative very well and doubles as a battle grid. I have another two players from a 2nd Ed game who may want to dive back in, but we're still enjoying OWoD Mage, so it may be awhile.<br /> <br /> The lack of releases sucks, but I've made liberal use of fan splats (thank you, Crumplepunch!), and the nature of my game over its first 6 months hasn't required a lot of content beyond what I'm providing myself (isolated setting with a very unusual set of problems). I'd like to be a player, even online (I'm primarily the ST for my groups), though I'm not sure I have the time for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12765-otto-d-fey","name":"Otto D'Fey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-01T04:31:00-07:00","id":1315852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1094031-how-big-is-the-exalted-playerbase-these-days?p=1095282#post1095282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bIt would have been great if the lesson that &amp;quot;the forums have rules of conduct that you agreed to abide by when you signed up&amp;quot; had been the lesson learned when warnings were issued. Unfortunately certain people felt they were above those rules or that the rules didn't apply to them. We made it very clear that the behavior seen near the end of the old WW forums was not going to be allowed here because it absolutely drove people away from participating on those forums. I would know because I read all the reports from users who were sick of being attacked for daring to disagree with some forum superstar. Stating the moderation caused problems rather than people who couldn't engage others within the rules of conduct is absolutely bullshit.</div> </div> </div> </div>In for an obol in for a talent.<br /> <br /> So the old WW forums had toxic users who drove people away. Not the conduct of the mods, it was the conduct of the rule breakers.<br /> <br /> These forums are strictly moderated and the toxic users who were solely responsible for driving people away aren't allowed.<br /> <br /> Crazed conspiracy theorists make the &quot;bullshit&quot; claim that over moderation causes problems.<br /> <br /> So... the claim is that these forums are more active than the old WW forums? What with it being better moderated and not having toxic users driving people away? 'Cause that's a pretty bold claim when stacked against Piff's &quot;bullshit&quot;.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> But to the actual point, with The Realm out, I'd like to run a game. Does anyone have any thoughts on estimating the current size of the playerbase? Or ideas on how to boost the playerbase? Or tactics for running a PbP game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-02T12:02:16-07:00","id":1316133,"title":"","content":"I'm locking this. Darksider can respond to you arging with something he said two years ago if he wants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}